+  // The tierless port — the whole thing (docs/corpus.md rung 3). `api` is the app's
+  // single API client: services, hooks and the whole interceptor chain sit above it and
+  // are untouched, and only the I/O bottom under them changes. Every same-origin request
+  // becomes one exec crossing on a single ws session to the gateway on <page-port>+100;
+  // browser-pinned configs (progress, blob, FormData bodies) fall through to axios's own
+  // adapter. Installed here rather than at `axios.create` so the crossing's exec is bound
+  // to the resolved API host; idempotent, so the host-switch path re-runs harmlessly.
+  //
+  // Both relaxations are load-bearing for this app and are why they exist: InvenTree sets
+  // `withCredentials` and a 5000 ms `timeout` on EVERY request, and each is pinned by
+  // default. The gateway runs with --cookie-authority, which is what makes the session
+  // cookie reproducible on the other tier; the deadline is enforced in the adapter.
+  tierlessAxios(axios, api, { crossCredentialed: true, crossTimeouts: true });
